# EIS is a private, file-native repository. Almost everything here is
# deliberately tracked: core context, the decision journal, and dossiers ARE
# the product, and their history is the learning mechanism (ADR-002).
#
# Only machine noise belongs here. If you are about to ignore a .md file,
# you are probably making a mistake.

# OS artifacts
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Claude Code machine-local state. Note that .claude/ itself is NOT ignored:
# shared commands and settings are part of the system.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Business Memory — your company's private knowledge (ADR-010).
#
# Ignored by default because this repository is open source: the likeliest
# accident is pushing a fork and publishing your cash position and runway.
# That is irreversible. The update workflow preserves prior values as in-file
# history lines, so the evolution of your understanding survives regardless.
#
# To version it anyway (recommended if your remote is private and yours
# alone), delete the next line.
core/business_memory.md

# Scratch work that is not a decision record
scratch/
*.tmp
